            "description": "Apply logarithm properties",
            "template": "Simplify log({a}) + log({b}) - log({c})",
            "note": "Use combination of product, quotient, and power rules"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "conicSections": {
      "title": "Conic Sections",
      "description": "Curves formed by intersecting a plane with a cone: circles, ellipses, parabolas, and hyperbolas",
      "concepts": [
        {
          "name": "Circle",
          "explanation": "Set of points equidistant from a center. Standard form: \\((x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2\\)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "problem": "Find the center and radius of \\(x^2 + y^2 - 4x + 6y - 12 = 0\\)",
              "solution": "Center: \\((2, -3)\\), Radius: 5",
              "steps": [
                "Group x and y terms: \\((x^2 - 4x) + (y^2 + 6y) = 12\\)",
                "Complete the square for x: \\(x^2 - 4x + 4 = (x - 2)^2\\)",
                "Complete the square for y: \\(y^2 + 6y + 9 = (y + 3)^2\\)",
                "Add to both sides: \\((x - 2)^2 + (y + 3)^2 = 12 + 4 + 9 = 25\\)",
                "Center: \\((2, -3)\\), Radius: \\(\\sqrt{25} = 5\\)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Ellipse",
          "explanation": "Set of points where the sum of distances to two foci is constant. Standard form: \\(\\dfrac{(x - h)^2}{a^2} + \\dfrac{(y - k)^2}{b^2} = 1\\)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "problem": "Find the vertices and foci of \\(\\dfrac{x^2}{25} + \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1\\)",
              "solution": "Vertices: \\((\\pm 5, 0)\\), Foci: \\((\\pm 4, 0)\\)",
              "steps": [
                "\\(a^2 = 25\\), so \\(a = 5\\) (major axis along x)",
                "\\(b^2 = 9\\), so \\(b = 3\\) (minor axis along y)",
                "Vertices on the major axis: \\((\\pm 5, 0)\\)",
                "\\(c^2 = a^2 - b^2 = 25 - 9 = 16\\), so \\(c = 4\\)",
                "Foci: \\((\\pm 4, 0)\\)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Parabola",
          "explanation": "Set of points equidistant from a focus and directrix. Standard form: \\((x - h)^2 = 4p(y - k)\\)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "problem": "Find the vertex, focus, and directrix of \\(y^2 = 8x\\)",
              "solution": "Vertex: \\((0, 0)\\), Focus: \\((2, 0)\\), Directrix: \\(x = -2\\)",
              "steps": [
                "Standard form: \\(y^2 = 4px\\) with \\(4p = 8\\), so \\(p = 2\\)",
                "Vertex: \\((0, 0)\\)",
                "Focus: \\((p, 0) = (2, 0)\\)",
                "Directrix: \\(x = -p = -2\\)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Hyperbola",
          "explanation": "Set of points where the absolute difference of distances to two foci is constant. Standard form: \\(\\dfrac{(x - h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y - k)^2}{b^2} = 1\\)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "problem": "Find the vertices and asymptotes of \\(\\dfrac{x^2}{16} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1\\)",
              "solution": "Vertices: \\((\\pm 4, 0)\\), Asymptotes: \\(y = \\pm\\dfrac{3}{4}x\\)",
              "steps": [
                "\\(a^2 = 16\\), so \\(a = 4\\)",
                "\\(b^2 = 9\\), so \\(b = 3\\)",
                "Vertices: \\((\\pm 4, 0)\\)",
                "Asymptotes: \\(y = \\pm\\dfrac{b}{a}x = \\pm\\dfrac{3}{4}x\\)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "problemGenerator": {
        "types": [
          {
            "name": "circle_standard",
            "description": "Convert circle to standard form",
            "template": "x² + y² + {d}x + {e}y + {f} = 0",
            "note": "Complete the square"
          },
          {
            "name": "ellipse_properties",
            "description": "Find ellipse properties",
            "template": "(x² / {a}) + (y² / {b}) = 1",
            "note": "Find vertices and foci"
          },
          {
            "name": "parabola_standard",
            "description": "Identify parabola properties",
            "template": "{vertex_form}",
            "note": "Find vertex, focus, directrix"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "matrixAlgebra": {
      "title": "Matrix Algebra",
      "description": "Operations with matrices and solving systems using matrices",
      "concepts": [
        {
          "name": "Matrix Operations",
          "explanation": "Addition, subtraction, scalar multiplication, and matrix multiplication",
          "examples": [
            {
              "problem": "Find \\(AB\\) where \\(A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}\\) and \\(B = \\begin{bmatrix} 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 \\end{bmatrix}\\)",
              "solution": "\\(\\begin{bmatrix} 19 & 22 \\\\ 43 & 50 \\end{bmatrix}\\)",
              "steps": [
                "Multiply rows of A by columns of B",
                "Entry (1,1): \\((1 \\times 5) + (2 \\times 7) = 5 + 14 = 19\\)",
                "Entry (1,2): \\((1 \\times 6) + (2 \\times 8) = 6 + 16 = 22\\)",
                "Entry (2,1): \\((3 \\times 5) + (4 \\times 7) = 15 + 28 = 43\\)",
                "Entry (2,2): \\((3 \\times 6) + (4 \\times 8) = 18 + 32 = 50\\)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Determinants",
          "explanation": "A scalar value associated with a square matrix. For a 2×2 matrix: \\(\\det(A) = ad - bc\\)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "problem": "Find the determinant of \\(\\begin{bmatrix} 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}\\)",
              "solution": "10",
              "steps": [
                "For a 2×2 matrix \\(\\begin{bmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{bmatrix}\\), \\(\\det = ad - bc\\)",
                "\\(\\det = (3 \\times 4) - (2 \\times 1) = 12 - 2 = 10\\)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Matrix Inverse",
          "explanation": "For a 2×2 matrix, the inverse is \\(A^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det} \\begin{bmatrix} d & -b \\\\ -c & a \\end{bmatrix}\\)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "problem": "Find the inverse of \\(\\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}\\)",
              "solution": "\\(\\begin{bmatrix} 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}\\)",
              "steps": [
                "\\(\\det = (2 \\times 3) - (1 \\times 5) = 6 - 5 = 1\\)",
                "\\(A^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix} 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\end{bmatrix}\\)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "problemGenerator": {
        "types": [
          {
            "name": "matrix_multiply",
            "description": "Multiply two matrices",
            "template": "Multiply matrices A and B",
            "note": "Row of A · Column of B for each entry"
          },
          {
            "name": "determinant",
            "description": "Calculate determinant",
